My bags are heavy and full.
I need a break.
I go to a small cart.
A man sells drinks here.
"Good morning," I say.
"I would like a coffee, please."
The seller smiles.
"With milk and sugar?" he asks.
"Only with milk, please," I answer.
He gives me the coffee.
"How much is that?" I ask.
"That comes to three euros," the man says.
I give him the money.
I stand at a high table at the edge.
I put my two bags on the ground.
The coffee is warm and delicious.
I drink slowly.
Many people walk past.
The stalls are very colourful.
I like watching the people.
